## Optional: separate Terraform users per environment (dev vs prod)

Use different Snowflake users and RSA keys so CI audit logs and secrets stay separate. Terragrunt reads the login from env `SNOWFLAKE_USER` (default `TERRAFORM`).

For each user, repeat Step 1 with a distinct key file, then:

```
USE ROLE SECURITYADMIN;
CREATE USER TERRAFORM_DEV RSA_PUBLIC_KEY='<DEV_PUBLIC_KEY_ONE_LINE>' DEFAULT_ROLE=PUBLIC MUST_CHANGE_PASSWORD=FALSE;
CREATE USER TERRAFORM_PROD RSA_PUBLIC_KEY='<PROD_PUBLIC_KEY_ONE_LINE>' DEFAULT_ROLE=PUBLIC MUST_CHANGE_PASSWORD=FALSE;

GRANT ROLE SYSADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM_DEV;
GRANT ROLE SECURITYADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM_DEV;
GRANT ROLE SYSADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM_PROD;
GRANT ROLE SECURITYADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM_PROD;
-- Optional, same as single-user flow:
-- GRANT ROLE ACCOUNTADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM_DEV;
-- GRANT ROLE ACCOUNTADMIN TO USER TERRAFORM_PROD;
```

Locally or in CI for dev stacks: `export SNOWFLAKE_USER=TERRAFORM_DEV` and the matching private key. For prod: `SNOWFLAKE_USER=TERRAFORM_PROD` and its key.